      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/temporary/28609993-b1fe-4533-b1b5-8e926ae00b1d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/fr/download-our-new-free-reconciliaction-calendar/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Politique en matière d'IA chez DWF        "
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund des technologies d'intelligence artificielle sécurisées et spécialement conçues pour améliorer la manière dont nous fournissons des ressources et soutenons notre réseau. Ces outils permettent de maintenir les informations à jour à l'aide de données accessibles au public, ce qui réduit les délais, minimise le gaspillage et garantit que les ressources parviennent bien à leur destinataire. Le respect de la vie privée est primordial ; aucune information personnelle n'est partagée en dehors du DWF, et vous pouvez vous désinscrire à tout moment.\n            "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/temporary/cd361089-91bb-48a6-ade2-fb79ae5208ab",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/fr/download-our-new-free-reconciliaction-calendar/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "À propos de DWF\nInspiré par l’histoire de Chanie et par l’appel de Gord à bâtir un Canada meilleur, le Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund à favoriser la compréhension culturelle et Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund ouvrir la voie à la réconciliation entre les peuples autochtone et non autochtones. Notre objectif est d’améliorer la vie des autochtone en sensibilisant la population, en favorisant l’éducation et en tissant des liens entre tous les peuples du Canada.\nAbonnez-vous à notre newsletter\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/temporary/3434aab3-43a8-4460-bf70-abc782f9bdfc",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/fr/download-our-new-free-reconciliaction-calendar/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Contactez-nous\nE-mail : staff@downiewenjack.ca\nNuméro gratuit : 1-833-666-2414 \nNuméro local : 519-964-0393 \nAdresse :\nBoîte postale 749\nOHSWEKEN, ON\nN0A1M0\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g2584880",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Download our new, free ReconciliACTION Calendar!\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g2584920",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/ImageObject"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/digitalcalendar.jpg"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g2584960",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "You can download your free digital copy of the bilingual ReconciliACTION Calendar today!\nDWF aims to build cultural understanding and create a path toward reconciliation between Indigenous and non-Indigenous peoples. One of the ways we promote understanding and connection is by sharing important cultural resources, like this calendar.\nAbout the calendar\n\nThe Anishinaabe calendar is deeply rooted in the cycles of the moon. The turtle shell is a visual match for the days and moons in a lunar year: the outer ring of the shell has small scales representing the 28 days in a lunar month, while the larger scales in the center symbolize the 13 moons of the year. Each of these moons is named after a natural event that takes place during that time.\nSpanning from September 2024 to August 2025, the calendar takes an important step toward decolonization by focusing on Indigenous dates of significance—dates that are important to the histories, cultures, and traditions of Indigenous peoples – rather than colonial dates.\nThe calendar also highlights Legacy Schools reconciliACTIONs— actions taken by classrooms, schools, and groups throughout Canada to move reconciliation forward. We hope that these reconciliACTIONS inspire you to engage in your own meaningful actions that support reconciliation.\nHow DWF Moves Reconciliation Forward\nThe Legacy Schools program is a national initiative offering free resources to Educators and youth group leaders to help them teach not only the true history of Canada, but also the richness, strength, and resilience of Indigenous cultures.\nThe ReconciliACTION Calendar is just one example of the resources we offer to educators and organizations in their toolkits. It serves as an educational tool that helps to deepen understanding and inspire action to help bridge the gap between Indigenous and non-Indigenous people. By engaging with the calendar, you’re not only enriching your own understanding but advancing our collective journey towards reconciliation.\nLooking for more ways to help?\n\nSpread the word: Share this link with family and friends to download their own copy of the calendar.\nDonate: Your support allows us to continue to create resources such as the ReconciliACTION calendar to be used in schools and offices from coast to coast to coast. Donate here.\nBecome a Legacy School: Educators and youth group leaders can learn more about our Legacy Schools program and sign up to receive resources for your classroom.\nBecome a Legacy Space: Create a safe, welcoming place in your office where conversations and education about the true history of Canada and our collective journey toward reconciliation are encouraged and supported. Learn more.\nTake ReconciliACTION: Whether it’s hosting a fundraiser, learning about Indigenous history, or supporting Indigenous artists, take reconciliACTION and share it with DWF!\n\n"
      }
    ]
  },
