  {
    "@id": "_:g5981720",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Wine Rack Continues Partnership with Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund for Fourth Year\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g5981760",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Toronto, ON (August 28, 2024) – As the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation on September 30 approaches, Wine Rack proudly announces its fourth consecutive year of partnership with the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund (DWF). Over the past three years, Wine Rack stores across Ontario have collectively raised over $250,000 in support of DWF, an Indigenous-led national charity that aims to build cultural understanding and create a path toward reconciliation between Indigenous and non-Indigenous peoples.\nFrom September 1-30, 2024, visit your local Wine Rack store to donate to the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund to support their efforts to build awareness, education, and connections between all peoples in Canada. 100% of funds raised will be donated to DWF.\nWine Rack will extend its commitment to reconciliation by inviting all Arterra Wines Canada employees to participate in Walk for Wenjack during Secret Path Week (October 17-22, 2024). In addition, a range of learning opportunities will be offered to enhance understanding and foster awareness of Indigenous cultures and history.\n“Our ongoing partnership with the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund is a testament to our collective dedication to reconciliation,” said Will Meijer, Executive Vice President, Sales at Arterra Wines Canada. “We are honoured to continue this journey through the in-store campaign, and our engagement in Walk for Wenjack and other educational initiatives reflects our commitment to learning and growing together.”\nSarah Midanik, President & CEO of the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund, added, “The support from Wine Rack and its employees has been instrumental in advancing our mission. Their continued dedication helps uphold the legacies of Gord Downie and Chanie Wenjack while driving meaningful change. Miigwetch for your commitment to reconciliation and for inspiring others to join this crucial journey toward a better future.”\nWine Rack and Arterra Wines Canada look forward to another impactful year of partnership and encourage all to participate in this meaningful cause, enhancing collective efforts toward reconciliation.\nAbout the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund\nInspired by Chanie’s story and Gord’s call to build a better Canada, the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund aims to build cultural understanding and create a path toward reconciliation between Indigenous and non-Indigenous peoples. Our goal is to improve the lives of Indigenous people by building awareness, education, and connections between all peoples in Canada. Learn more at downiewenjack.ca.\nAbout Wine Rack\nWith more than 164 wine boutiques conveniently located throughout Ontario, Wine Rack provides a breadth of quality Ontario and International Canadian Blended wines for any occasion. It carries over 150 products from well-known brands such as Jackson-Triggs, Inniskillin, Saintly, Bask, OPEN, Bodacious, Naked Grape, Growers Cider, Cartier Irish Cream and many more. Wine Rack employs approximately 1,000 staff across Ontario and is the retail division of Arterra Wines Canada, Inc. For more information about Wine Rack, visit Winerack.com\nAbout Arterra\nArterra Wines Canada, Inc. is the country’s leading producer and marketer of award-winning, globally recognized Canadian and imported wines. Arterra is headquartered in Mississauga, ON, and operates eight wineries across the country, with over 1,700 acres of premium vineyards in Canada’s wine regions. For more information about Arterra Wines Canada, Inc., visit www.arterracanada.com.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
