      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Get In Touch\nE-mail: staff@downiewenjack.ca\nToll-free: 1-833-666-2414\nLocal: 519-964-0393\nAddress:\nPO BOX 749\nOHSWEKEN, ON\nN0A1M0\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g6471600",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/ImageObject"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://downiewenjack.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Holiday2025_WebBanner.jpg"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g6471620",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF Holiday Gift Guide – Moving Reconciliation Forward\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g6471660",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This holiday season, take #reconciliACTION by purchasing gifts from DWF’s Holiday Gift Guide. This guide features Indigenous-owned businesses, with options for all budgets and preferences. There is something meaningful for every person on your list!\n\n\nDWF – Merch Shop\nAbout: All proceeds from DWF’s merch store go to the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund and support our work to build cultural understanding and create a path toward reconciliation between Indigenous and non-Indigenous peoples. \nShop DWF’s Merch Store\n\n\nIshkōdé Records – Indigenous Artists on Vinyl\nAbout: As an Indigenous and women-owned record label, Ishkōdé Records was created to amplify Indigenous voices. You can support Indigenous artists by buying a vinyl for the music lover in your life.\nShop Indigenous Artists on Vinyl – Price: $30-35\n\n\nOutlier Leather Co. – Bucket Bag\nAbout: David Spence is Nisichawayasihk (Treaty 5) Cree and the founder of Outlier Leather Co. Every item is handcrafted by David and made with high quality, ethically sourced materials.\nAbout the product: “This bag is built to last, is naturally waterproof, and will develop a beautiful patina over time.”\nMore from Outlier Leather Co. | Shop the Bucket Bag – Price: $100\n\n\nIndigenous Roots Coffee Co. – Land Back Blend Medium/Dark\nAbout: The perfect gift for any coffee lover, Indigenous Roots Coffee Co. offers a wide variety of specialty coffees. Each coffee blend promotes reconciliation by supporting an Indigenous initiative.\nAbout the product: “Sweet & Comforting, this roast brings forward feelings of restoration and good medicine reflected in the name Land Back and represented by a mountain revealing the face of mother earth together with ravens on each side of her.“\nMore from Indigenous Roots Coffee Co. | Shop Land Back Medium/Dark – Price: $20.99\n\n\nWabanaki Maple – Barrel Aged Toasted Oak Maple Syrup\nAbout: Wabanaki Maple is an Indigenous female-owned business offering “a taste of our land’s cultural fabric’’ through their maple products. In addition to creating tasty fusions, Wabanaki Maple is committed to helping preserve our environment and helping Indigenous communities thrive. \nAbout the product: “A roasted thick flavour with honeyed overtones, this maple is painstakingly refined and aged to perfection, producing a syrup made unique with the time-honoured taste of lightly charred oak.”\nMore from Wabanaki Maple | Shop the Barrel Aged Toasted Oak Maple Syrup – Price: $14.95 – $30.95\n\n\nRoots + Raven – The Great Peace – Sleep Support Bath Bomb\nAbout: Made with locally grown ingredients, Roots + Raven promotes healing and relaxation with their wide variety of natural products. Roots + Raven also participates in local community gardens to provide access to and knowledge on growing medicinal herbs.\nAbout the product: “Perfect for sleep support, calming your being and dream time.”\nMore from Roots + Raven | Shop the Great Peace – Sleep Support Bath Bomb – Price: $7-20\n\n\nCheekbone Beauty – Healing Lip Oil\nAbout: Cheekbone Beauty is one of Canada’s first Indigenous-owned and founded cosmetics companies. They are creating a space for Indigenous representation in the beauty industry with products are sustainable, vegan, and cruelty-free.\nAbout the product: “Our Healing Lip Oils are infused with soothing peppermint oil and hyaluronic acid to provide your lips with the ultimate care and hydration they deserve. Brought to you in flattering and universal tones, these shades are designed to enhance every skin tone and style.”\nCheekbone Beauty | Healing Lip Oil – Price: $29\n\n\nIndigenous Box – Kinship Feast Collection – The Sharing\nAbout: Started in 2021, Indigenous Box connects Indigenous entrepreneurs to new customers worldwide. Discover Indigenous businesses and products with Indigenous Box!    \nAbout the product: “It is meant to be opened at the table, where stories are told, laughter flows, and meals bring comfort. Each piece represents reciprocity nourishment drawn from the land, shared in gratitude. It’s a reminder that what we give from the heart always comes back in kindness.” \nMore from Indigenous Box | Shop the Kinship Feast Collection – The Sharing – Price: $69\n\n\nMINI TIPI – Fleurs Indigenous Tote Bag\nAbout: MINI TIPI is a lifestyle brand that celebrates Indigenous arts and culture. They specialize high-quality textiles designed by Indigenous artists and manufactured locally in Gatineau, Québec. Through a portion of their sales, MINI TIPI raises money Indigenous initiatives and organizations including the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund. \nAbout the product: “It’s perfectly oversized for you to bring along for a day at the beach, your yoga or workout class, grabbing a few things at the grocery store, work or even some toys for the park!”\nMore from MINI TIPI | Shop the Fleurs Indigenous Tote Bag – Price: $70\n\n\nSisters Sage – Smokeless Smudge Spray\nAbout: Recognized as Indigenous Business of the Year 2022, Sisters Sage is a wellness brand built on Indigenous knowledge. Their products are made using traditional ingredients such as Cedar, Sage and Sweetgrass. \nAbout the product: “This beautiful blend of Sweetgrass and Tobacco leaf fragrance will leave you feeling refreshed. Our reusable glass bottles are convenient to take with you in your purse, bag, or to leave in your car.”\nMore from Sisters Sage | Shop the Smokeless Smudge Spray – Price: $22\n\n\nShades of Gray – Pet Treat Bundle\nAbout: Don’t forget about our furry friends this holiday season. Shades of Gray is family-owned business offering high quality rabbit treats. All natural and with only one ingredient, Shades of Gray pet treats support the health of your pet. \nAbout the product: “Looking for healthy, natural rabbit meat pet treats made in Canada? Our Shades of Gray Pet Treat Bundle – best sellers are featured and contain a variety of premium rabbit meat treats, perfect for dogs and cats of all sizes and life stages.”\nMore from Shades of Gray | Shop the Pet Treat Bundle – Price: $69.99\n\n\nPatrick Hunter – Holographic Eagle Feather\nAbout: Patrick Hunter is a two-spirit, Ojibwe painter, entrepreneur, and graphic designer from Red Lake, Ontario. He takes inspiration from his homeland and believes that a better world can be created through art, where future generations can see themselves reflected in mainstream culture.\nAbout the product: “Enjoy the reflections of Patrick’s Eagle Feather painting, now available as a print with holographic foil.”\nMore from Patrick Hunter | Shop Holographic Eagle Feather – Price: $150\n\n\nAwasis Boutique – The Matriarch\nAbout: Created by a mother of two, Awasis Boutique offers a wide selection of Indigenous designs for everyone of all ages. Awasis means “child” in Cree, which pays homage to creator Christine Marie’s Métis and Filipino roots.\nAbout the product: “Designed with our Métis Matriarchs in mind. Remembering how they made family, community and preserving their Métis Culture a valuable priority.” \nMore from Awasis Boutique | Shop The Matriarch – Price: $70\n\n\nSmudge the Blades – Cree Syllabics Hoodie\nAbout: Started by First Nations hockey player Harlan Kingfisher, Smudge the Blades celebrates First Nations hockey culture. Smudge the Blades gives back to the community by using a portion of proceeds to supply First Nations youth nationwide with new hockey equipment.\nAbout the product: “Smudge the Blades in Cree Syllabics! Available in youth and adult sizes.”\nMore from Smudge the Blades | Shop the Cree Syllabics Hoodie – Price: $60\n\n\nSi’st Sipu – Bear Grease Lilac Lotion Bar\nAbout: As an Indigenous-owned and operated business, Si’st Sipu creates skincare and wellness products using traditional plant knowledge as well as modern science. They offer hair care and skincare products all made with organic and wildcrafted ingredients. \nAbout the product: “Our bear grease lotion bar contains a blend of hydration rich cocoa butter, shea butter, babassu oil and bear grease. These emollients soften and soothe dry skin. They cover the skin with a protective film that traps moisture.”\nMore from Si’st Sipu | Shop the Bear Grease Lilac Lotion Bar – Price: $21\n\n\nBangin’ Bannock – Dry Mix\nAbout: Experience a taste of Indigenous culture with Bangin’ Bannock. From their signature frybread mix to sharing unique recipes and twists, they offer a great way to bring this tradition right to you!\nAbout the product: “Enjoy the timeless taste of tradition with our 400g Bangin’ Bannock dry mix. Perfect for both newcomers and seasoned bannock lovers, our mix brings the celebrated cultural food of Turtle Island right to your kitchen.”\nMore from Bangin’ Bannock | Shop Bangin’ Bannock Dry Mix – Price: $11.99\n\n\nMelissa Peter-Paul – DIY Quill Kit\nAbout: Melissa Peter-Paul is a Mi’kmaw Quill Artist from Abegweit First Nation. Located in P.E.I., Melissa sells a variety of her beautiful quill artwork and aims to revitalize the traditional artform. \nAbout the product: “You will learn how to make an 8 pointed star design with porcupine quills, birch bark and sweetgrass.”\nMore from Melissa Peter-Paul | Shop DIY Quill Kit – Price: $100\n\n\nInuky Glass Art & Engraving Inc. – Inuk Puzzle\nAbout: Every piece from Inuky Glass Art & Engraving Inc. is designed by Inuit artist and published children’s author, Raeann Brown. They offer a wide range of products including, decor, apparel, jewelry, and more!\nAbout the product: “Another unique creation! Our Inuk Puzzles are educational and artistic. Carefully designed from original drawings out of my children’s book Do You Wanna Build An Igloo? Inuttitut and English translations. Our puzzles are the perfect addition to any child’s puzzle collection.”\nMore from Inuky Glass Art & Engraving Inc. | Shop Inuk Puzzle – Price: $34.99\n\n\nMother Earth Essentials – Mother Earth: Plants for Health & Beauty\nAbout:  Mother Earth Essentials is rooted in traditional Indigenous knowledge and offers natural beauty products made with Canadian plants. In their store you can find all your beauty needs including soaps, shampoos, skincare and more!\nAbout the product: “Mother Earth Plants for Health & Beauty is a guide and recipe book to help you improve your life with ethically crafted health and beauty products that you can make at home. Within its pages, you’ll find out how to create a luxurious and natural beauty regime by crafting your own lotions, soaps and teas from all-natural ingredients.”\nMore from Mother Earth | Shop Mother Earth: Plants for Health & Beauty – Price: $24.95\n\nLuke Swinson – “Diindiisi-Blue Jay” Limited Edition Art Print\nAbout: A member of the Mississaugas of Scugog Island First Nation, Luke’s work reflects his desire to better understand and reclaim his Indigenous culture. He seeks to promote cultural education and preservation through his art projects.\nAbout the product: “11×14″, 0.75″ white border on textured paper (Canson Infinity Aquarelle 310gsm). Prints are signed, dated and numbered /250. Prints are enclosed in plastic sleeves and shipped in hard mailers for protection.”\nMore from Luke Swinson | Shop “Diindsi-Blue Jay” Limited Edition Art Print – Price: $70\n"
      }
    ]
  },
