    "@id": "_:g6831840",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF Holiday Gift Guide – Moving Reconciliation Forward\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g6831880",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This holiday season, take #reconciliACTION by purchasing gifts from DWF’s Holiday Gift Guide. This guide features Indigenous-owned businesses, a new merch collab with DWF Artist Ambassador Violet Gatensby , and of course, HBC’s iconic Point Blankets, which support Oshki Wupoowane | The Blanket Fund. With options for all budgets and preferences, there is something meaningful for every person on your list.\n\n\nDWF – Merch Shop\nAbout: All proceeds from DWF’s merch store go to the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund and support our work to build cultural understanding and create a path toward reconciliation between Indigenous and non-Indigenous peoples. Check out our recent collaboration with DWF Artist Ambassador Violet Gatensby!\nAbout the product: Violet Gatensby is an inland Tlingit artist from the Carcross/Tagish First Nation. A versatile and talented artist, Violet’s preferred medium is wood, but she also enjoys metalwork, designing, and painting. Her design, Strike a Match, is in honour of Chanie’s story and the thousands more children who never made it home from residential schools.\nShop DWF’s Merch Store\nPlease note: We are still shipping during the Canada Post strike. Your items will be shipped by FedEx.\n\n\nThe Bay – Point Blankets\nAbout the product: Net proceeds from the sale of HBC Point Blankets go toward Oshki Wupoowane | The Blanket Fund which supports Indigenous cultural, artistic, and educational activities. Check out some of the projects that have been funded so far through The Blanket Fund.\nShop the Bay Point Blankets – Price: $350\n\n\nMétis Branded – Deer Hide Men’s Vest\nAbout: Métis Branded was created by Casandra, a young, Indigenous entrepreneur, and mother of two who takes pride in making wonderful, one-of-a-kind pieces. Passionate about Métis culture and art, Casandra aims to repurpose vintage items, helping our planet. \nAbout the product: “This vest is created with repurposed deer hide and a hnd-woven sash; Styled with pockets in the front and fringe in the back, alongside a patterned blue back.”\nMore from Métis Branded | Shop the Deer Hide Men’s Vest – Price: $80\n\n\nUasau Soaps – Beach Glass Soap\nAbout: Hand-crafted using locally and sustainably sourced ingredients, Uasau Soaps highlights Inuit tradition through each step of its creations! These beautiful, small batch products aim to replenish and nurture your skin.\nAbout the product: “Our Beachglass Soap combines our other soaps into one olive-based soap. Each one is a unique kaleidoscope of fragments, like pebbles along a Frobisher Bay beach.“\nMore from Uasau Soaps | Shop Beach Glass Soap – Price: $15\n\n\nWabanaki Maple – Heritage Collection Mini Bundle Set\nAbout: Wabanaki Maple is an Indigenous female- owned business offering “a taste of our land’s cultural fabric’’ through their maple products. In addition to creating tasty fusions, Wabanaki Maple is committed to helping preserve our environment and helping Indigenous communities thrive. \nAbout the product: “This curated trio eatures three distinct maple syrups, each meticulously crafted to pay homage to the roots that have nourished us for generations: Chipotle Infused, Elderberry Infused, and Traditional Maple.”\nMore from Wabanaki Maple | Shop the Heritage Collection Mini Bundle Set – Price: $32\n\n\nThe Warrior Blends/Epices du Guerrier – Traditional Mix Gift Log\nAbout: Warrior Blends/Epices du Guerrier specializes in creating extraordinary spice blends that stem from Indigenous traditions and knowledge. They also prioritize giving back to the community, through their donations to food banks, youth centres, and more. \nAbout the product: “It’s good ! ‘O’YA’WIH! The ideal gift, real red pine log including 100g of our traditional blend and hand-wrapped by our craftsmen.”\nMore from The Warrior Blends/Epices du Guerrier | Shop the Traditional Mix Gift Log – Price: $30\n\n\nHi, love. Greetings – Flower Wreath Comfort and Joy: Wildflower Seed Paper Card\nAbout: Hi, love. Greetings is an Indigenous woman-owned small business located in Nova Scotia’s Annapolis Valley that creates handmade gifts designed for real life! Using eco-friendly materials, they offer unique gifts for anybody on your list.\nAbout the product: “The holidays are joyful and colourful with a festive floral wreath on this sustainable, plantable, and beautiful handmade seed paper greeting card. These adorable seed paper greeting cards are designed, printed, cut, and packaged by us on wildflower seed paper that’s made in Canada.”\nMore from Hi, love. Greetings | Shop the Flower Wreath Comfort and Joy: Wildflower Seed Paper Card – Price: $10\n\n\nJack59 – Amplify Giftset\nAbout: Jack59 proudly creates natural hair and body care products that are sustainably made and ethically sourced. In addition, each of their products is pH balanced, and created in a zero-waste production process. \nAbout the product: “The gift set includes an Amplify shampoo bar, Amplify conditioner bar, and a 100% backyard compostable shower container in the colour of your choice. You can use the bars to cleanse and condition your hair and body.” \nMore from Jack59 | Shop the Amplify Giftset – Price: $66\n\n\nLil Metis Shop in the Prairies – Alpaca Sweater\nAbout: Lil Metis Shop in the Prairies is a Métis-owned online retail shop offering modern takes on classic pieces! You can find everything from handmade jewelry to colouring pages, and more!\nAbout the product: These cozy sweaters are not only stylish, coming in a variety of colours and sizes, but are also made from 100% alpaca wool.\nMore from Lil Metis Shop in the Prairies | Shop the Alpaca Sweater – Price: $65\n\n\nSkwalwen – Sḵwálwen Botanicals Wellness Set\nAbout: With each product, Indigenous skincare brand Skwalwen aims to honor Skwxwú7mesh (Squamish) plant knowledge and tradition. Each of their creations has a Squamish name to honour where the tradition and knowledge comes from. \nAbout the product: “Featuring Sḵwálwen founder Leigh Joseph’s bestselling book Held by the Land, this set is complemented with products to help slow down, reflect, and relax.”\nMore from Skwalwen | Shop the Sḵwálwen Botanicals Wellness Set – Price: $98\n\n\nVictoria’s Arctic Fashion – VAF Hats\nAbout: Victoria’s Arctic Fashion creates handmade pieces that combine traditional Inuit sewing techniques with modern, and sustainably sourced fabrics. Created by Victoria Kakuktinniq, a proud Inuk woman, this business is based out of Nunavut. \nAbout the product: “A knit winter toque with or without fox fur pom poms and our leather VAF logo. The double layer makes it ideal for winter weather and outdoor activities.”\nMore from Victoria’s Arctic Fashion | Shop VAF Hats – Price: $88\n\n\nPatrick Hunter – “Ponder”\nAbout: Patrick Hunter is a two-spirit, Ojibwe painter, entrepreneur, and graphic designer from Red Lake, Ontario. He takes inspiration from his homeland and believes that a better world can be created through art, where future generations can see themselves reflected in mainstream culture.\nAbout the product: This beautiful piece by Patrick Hunter is titled “Ponder”. \nMore from Patrick Hunter | Shop “Ponder” – Price: $75\n\n\nAwasis Boutique – Full Size Blankets\nAbout: Created by a mother of two, Awasis Boutique offers a wide selection of Indigenous designs for everyone of all ages. Awasis means “child” in Cree, which pays homage to creator Christine Marie’s Métis and Filipino roots.\nAbout the product: “These full-size blankets are made using poly and Sherpa ultra soft fabrics featuring our very own custom, authentic Indigenous designs.” \n“$5 (SMALL) and $10 (LRG) from every blanket sold with the orange florals will be donated to the Legacy of Hope Foundation to help support residential school Survivors and their families.”\nMore from Awasis Boutique | Shop Full Size Blankets – Price: $90\n\n\nIndigenous PEI – Clay Diffuser\nAbout: More than just a store,’ Indigenous PEI holds focus on the stories, cultural heritage, and inspiration of the artwork and products that they offer. While hosting an array of artisans, they also aim to create a space for reconciliation to grow.\nAbout the product: “Handmade clay diffuser with double curve design, included with peppermint essential oil and gift box. Artisans Dana & Tess Wigmore, a mother and daughter team from Manitoba now residing on Epekwitk, get their inspiration from Cree and Mi’kmaq culture.”\nMore from Indigenous PEI | Shop the Clay Diffuser – Price: $32.99\n\n\nYukon Soaps – Labrador Tea Bath Salts\nAbout: As an Indigenous-owned and operated business, Yukon Soaps creates products that are infused and imprinted with the spirit of the Yukon. They offer beautiful products such as soap bars, body scrubs, and more! \nAbout the product: “Elevate your bathing routine with our Labrador Tea Bath Salts. Lovingly crafted with hand-harvested labrador tea leaves and essential oils of spruce and yarrow for a deeply relaxing experience. The aromatic scent is often described as herbal and earthy, transporting you to the serene wilderness of the Yukon.”\nMore from Yukon Soaps | Shop Labrador Tea Bath Salts – Price: $15.00\n\n\nBangin’ Bannock – Dry Mix\nAbout: Experience a taste of Indigenous culture with Bangin Bannock. From their signature frybread mix to sharing unique recipes and twists, they offer a great way to bring this tradition right to you!\nAbout the product: “Enjoy the timeless taste of tradition with our 400g Bangin’ Bannock dry mix. Perfect for both newcomers and seasoned bannock lovers, our mix brings the celebrated cultural food of Turtle Island right to your kitchen.”\nMore from Bangin’ Bannock | Shop Bangin’ Bannock Dry Mix – Price: $11.99\n"
      }
    ]
  },
