    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7550640",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "On May 28, we learned about the heartbreaking discovery of 215 children buried at a former residential school on Tk’emlúps te Secwépemc territory in Kamloops, BC. We stand with the Secwépemc community, all the families and communities of these young children, and all those impacted by residential schools in their grief. “It’s really hard when we know what they are going through. We always knew findings would come out one day.” said Daisy Munroe, Chanie Wenjack’s eldest sister.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tA statement from DWF\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7550720",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Toronto Star – Students from JA Laird Elementary School have welcomed community feedback from businesses in the Columbia Valley, and even from some residential school survivors, on a recent school project.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tSchool project garners accolades from community | Toronto Star\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7550800",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Following a successful meeting on Dec. 5, 2020, the Educator Advisory Committee will meet again in March. Despite the difficult and unusual school year, our Legacy Schools have done great work in their efforts towards reconciliation. Their hard work and dedication has inspired our committee to continue to work as hard as possible – despite the circumstances – to improve and add to our Legacy Schools Program. We’re extremely proud to introduce two new members to our committee.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tThe Educator Advisory Committee Welcomes New Members\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7550880",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CTV News – Canada’s top doubles luge team had to get creative in order to find a new sponsor to help fund their 2021 World Cup season.\nTristan Walker and Justin Snith are getting ready to head to Germany to start their World Cup season to compete in three World Cups and a world championship in January and like all high performance athletes, the dynamic luge duo rely on sponsorship deals to help finance their World Cup and Olympic dreams – most years.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tCanada’s top doubles luge team gets creative to fill sponsorship role | CTV News\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7550960",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Oshawa Express – The first four episodes are available now, featuring guests such as Regional Chair John Henry; CEO of the Ontario Chamber of Commerce Rocco Rossi; Executive Director and Co-Head of the Toronto International Film Festival Joana Vicente; and President and CEO of the Gord Downie and Chanie Wenjack Fund Sarah Midanik.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tDurham to host new podcast series | Oshawa Express\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7551040",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Timmins Today – Moosonee Public School (MPS) has taken the next step in raising awareness about residential schools by registering to be a Legacy School.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tMoosonee Public School joins Legacy School program | Timmins Today\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7551120",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "North Bay Nugget – Percy Baxter Middle School is now considered a legacy school with the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tPercy Baxter named legacy school through Downie-Wenjack Fund | North Bay Nugget\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7551200",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This past week many of our Legacy Schools took part in Secret Path Week, a week-long event that is held from October 17th to October 22nd to honour the passing of Gord Downie and Chanie Wenjack. Throughout the school year, and especially during Secret Path Week, we encourage our Legacy School educators and students to take part in reconciliACTIONs. These are meaningful actions that work towards reconciliation, creating awareness, learning and sharing to create strong relationships among all Canadians.\nWe would love to acknowledge some of the great reconciliACTIONs that have been led by  Legacy Schools not only during Secret Path Week but throughout the 2020 school year. We hope their powerful actions  inspire you and those around you to get involved and #DoSomething.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tReconciliACTIONs At Legacy Schools\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7551280",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "NWMO – The Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund (DWF) and the Nuclear Waste Management Organization (NWMO) today announced plans to work together to create a meaningful pathway for Reconciliation.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tThe Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund and the Nuclear Waste Management Organization Announce Five-Year Partnership for Orange Shirt Day | NWMO\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7551360",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Early in May, we challenged our Legacy Schools students to design posters that answer the question “What does it mean to be an Indigenous Ally?” They definitely rose to the occasion! We loved all of the posters that were submitted, and it was certainly difficult to select the winners from elementary, middle, and secondary schools. Winners will receive a prize pack from DWF and appear in our Legacy Schools calendar for 2020-2021.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tCongratulations to the Legacy Schools Poster Contest Winners!\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DWF"
      }
    ]
  },
