      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805240",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Each year on April 7, World Health Day raises awareness of global health issues and promotes access to quality healthcare for all. In Canada, this includes recognizing that equitable access to healthcare has not been a reality for Indigenous children, particularly First Nations children living on reserve. Jordan’s Principle exists because of this inequity.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tWorld Health Day: Honouring Equity Through Jordan’s Principle\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805320",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Independent Assessment Process (IAP) and earlier Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) were compensation processes established under the Indian Residential Schools Settlement Agreement (IRSSA) for Survivors who experienced abuse in residential schools in Canada. Under a Supreme Court decision, IAP and ADR records are scheduled to be destroyed on September 19, 2027, unless a Survivor chooses otherwise. This timeline is part of a legal ruling to protect privacy and confidentiality.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tUnderstanding the Options for IRSSA Records\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805400",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Secret Path celebrates its ten-year anniversary of the project’s release this year. It has been sixty years since Chanie Wenjack’s death. The Secret Path was created by songwriter Gord Downie. This was his last project created before his unfortunate passing in 2017.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tThe Secret Path: A Film of Commemoration | The Chronicle\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805480",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "On Tuesday, March 24, you can take in the Madwewetoon Indigenous Music & Arts Festival at Knox Hall, an evening celebrating Indigenous artists. The all ages show is pay-what-you-can and is a collaboration between the Gord Downie & Chanie Wenjack Fund (DWF) and Canada’s Music Incubator (CMI).\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tPay-what-you-can Indigenous music festival hits Knox Hall Mar. 24 | Sudbury.com\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805560",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In 2025, Ontario Teachers’ reaffirmed our commitment to fostering inclusion and reconciliation through the development of our Indigenous Action Plan (IAP), a first-of-its-kind initiative among Canadian pension plans.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tAdvancing reconciliation through partnership and action\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805640",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "International Women’s Day 2026 calls for Rights. Justice. Action. For ALL Women and Girls. This theme recognizes that advancing equality requires structural change, sustained advocacy, and leadership rooted in community. Today and every day, we honour Indigenous women throughout the world who are advancing human rights, protecting lands and waters, strengthening communities, and shaping international policy. Their leadership reflects generations of resilience, responsibility, and action.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tInternational Women’s Day 2026 | Rights. Justice. Action. For ALL Women and Girls\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805720",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "On March 12 at 7:30 p.m., Wayne Kaulbach will be celebrating the music, the life, and the legacy of Gord Downie with his ‘One Man Tragically Hip Cover Band’.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tPut some spring in your step with stellar entertainment at the Showroom this March | Cowichan Valley Citizen\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805800",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Millennial Scoop refers to the ongoing crisis of Indigenous children being disproportionately removed from their families and communities by child welfare systems. This is a continuation of harms seen in the Sixties Scoop era, where Indigenous children were taken and placed in non‑Indigenous care, with devastating effects on identity, culture, and family ties. \n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tMillennial Scoop, Bill C‑92, and Indigenous Child Welfare\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805880",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Bill 5, officially titled the Protect Ontario by Unleashing our Economy Act, 2025, was passed by the Ontario government on June 5, 2025. The legislation makes major changes to 10 provincial laws, including the repeal of the Endangered Species Act, 2007, the Ontario Place Corporation Act, and the creation of a new Special Economic Zones Act.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tLearn About Bill 5\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7805960",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Canadore College hosted its inaugural Walk for Wenjack on Friday, Dec. 5. Thirty participants completed laps inside the Canadore Dome at the Commerce Court Campus, raising more than $1,200 in support of the Gord Downie and Chanie Wenjack Fund (DWF).\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\tCanadore hosts its first-ever ‘Walk for Wenjack’ last Friday | North Bay Nugget\t\t\t\t"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/author": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "communications"
      }
    ]
  },
